{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_2026_09_10_vapi_mcp_on_the_third_provider", "label": "Vapi MCP on the Third Provider (note)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/2026-09-10-vapi-mcp-on-the-third-provider.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Vapi accepts an inline MCP tool, making it the cheapest of the three providers to grant; the credential is written into the assistant.", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_2026_09_10_vapi_mcp_on_the_third_provider_inline_model_tools", "label": "Inline model.tools MCP block (not toolIds)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/2026-09-10-vapi-mcp-on-the-third-provider.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A stored tool would add a second remote object with its own id, hash, lockfile entry and ordering problem; inline puts the grant inside vapiHash.", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_2026_09_10_vapi_mcp_on_the_third_provider_mcp_token_in_assistant", "label": "MCP_TOKEN written into Vapi assistant headers", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/2026-09-10-vapi-mcp-on-the-third-provider.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Vapi's public API has no credential endpoints, so the token is written in the clear; credentialId is the upgrade path.", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_2026_09_10_vapi_mcp_on_the_third_provider_missing_token_skips_provider", "label": "Missing MCP_TOKEN skips Vapi driver", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/2026-09-10-vapi-mcp-on-the-third-provider.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A sync without the token would PATCH the live assistant with an empty Bearer and every tool call would 401 silently, so the provider is made unavailable() instead.", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_2026_09_10_vapi_mcp_on_the_third_provider_mcpserverids_bug", "label": "mcpServerIds ElevenLabs-only bug in buildPlan", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/2026-09-10-vapi-mcp-on-the-third-provider.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "mcpServerIdsFor was keyed on grant set alone and applied to every driver, which would cause an endless PATCH loop for words-3.1.", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_2026_09_10_vapi_mcp_on_the_third_provider_words_3_1", "label": "words-3.1 prompt version", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/2026-09-10-vapi-mcp-on-the-third-provider.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Kept as a new module rather than editing 3.0 so the same lesson stays byte-identical across three services for comparison.", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_2026_09_10_vapi_mcp_on_the_third_provider_mcp_url_guard", "label": "mcp-url.ts shared URL guard", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/2026-09-10-vapi-mcp-on-the-third-provider.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ElevenLabs and Vapi are the same shape (provisioned, shared with production), so the guard is shared instead of duplicated.", "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_2026_09_10_vapi_mcp_on_the_third_provider_anonymous_owner", "label": "MCP-saved words are anonymous (owner_id NULL)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/2026-09-10-vapi-mcp-on-the-third-provider.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null, "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "docs_2026_08_28_openai_realtime_mcp_tools", "label": "OpenAI Realtime MCP tools note", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/2026-09-10-vapi-mcp-on-the-third-pro